":"mcq","prompt":"Which atomic particle has a negative charge?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Whole nucleus","misconception":"chemistry.atoms.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Electron"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Proton","misconception":"chemistry.atoms.mixup.2.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Neutron","misconception":"chemistry.atoms.mixup.2.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Electrons carry negative charge. When an object gains them, its net charge becomes more negative.","scienceFact":"Electrons carry negative charge. When an object gains them, its net charge becomes more negative.","topic":"chemistry.atoms","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Atomic structure, elements and periodic patterns. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.atoms.e.003","deckId":"chemistry.atoms","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What does an element’s atomic number count?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"All nuclear particles","misconception":"chemistry.atoms.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Electron shells","misconception":"chemistry.atoms.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Protons"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Neutrons only","misconception":"chemistry.atoms.mixup.3.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"Atomic number is the number of protons. All atoms of one element have the same proton number.","scienceFact":"Atomic number is the number of protons. All atoms of one element have the same proton number.","topic":"chemistry.atoms","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Atomic structure, elements and periodic patterns. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.atoms.e.004","deckId":"chemistry.atoms","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the total number of protons and neutrons called?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Atomic number","misconception":"c