rops?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Melting","misconception":"chemistry.matter.mixup.7.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Sublimation","misconception":"chemistry.matter.mixup.7.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Evaporation","misconception":"chemistry.matter.mixup.7.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Condensation"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Water vapor can condense into liquid on a cool surface. The drops do not pass through the bottle wall.","scienceFact":"Water vapor can condense into liquid on a cool surface. The drops do not pass through the bottle wall.","topic":"chemistry.matter","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Properties, states, solutions and safe separation. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.matter.m.008","deckId":"chemistry.matter","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A student mixes iron filings and dry sand. Which material can be pulled out with a magnet?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Iron and sand"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Salt and water","misconception":"chemistry.matter.mixup.8.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Sugar and water","misconception":"chemistry.matter.mixup.8.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Oxygen and nitrogen","misconception":"chemistry.matter.mixup.8.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Iron is attracted to magnets. A magnet can separate iron pieces from materials such as dry sand.","scienceFact":"Iron is attracted to magnets. A magnet can separate iron pieces from materials such as dry sand.","topic":"chemistry.matter","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Properties, states, solutions and safe separation. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.matter.m.009","deckId":"chemistry.matter","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"Two equal-sized blocks have different masses. Which property compares their mass per volume?","op