no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"diagram":"beakers"},{"id":"chemistry.reactions.e.001","deckId":"chemistry.reactions","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What stays the same during a chemical reaction in a closed system?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Total mass"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Gas volume","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Temperature","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.1.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Number of molecules","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.1.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Atoms are conserved in a chemical reaction. Total mass stays the same in a closed system.","scienceFact":"Atoms are conserved in a chemical reaction. Total mass stays the same in a closed system.","topic":"chemistry.reactions","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Chemical change and conservation of mass. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.reactions.e.002","deckId":"chemistry.reactions","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is a common sign that new substances may have formed?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"The label is changed","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"A new gas forms"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"The cup is moved","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.2.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"A spoon is removed","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.2.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"New gas, a precipitate, or an unexpected energy change can be clues to a chemical reaction. Use more than one clue when needed.","scienceFact":"New gas, a precipitate, or an unexpected energy change can be clues to a chemical reaction. Use more than one clue when needed.","topic":"chemistry.reactions","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Chemical change and conservation of mass. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.reactions.e.003","deckId":"chemistry.reactions","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"Which process forms rust on iron in the Philippines’ humid air?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only evaporation","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Magnetic sorting","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Oxidation"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Simple melting","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.3.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"Rusting is oxidation of iron involving oxygen and water. Atoms from the air become part of the rust.","scienceFact":"Rusting is oxidation of iron involving oxygen and water. Atoms from the air become part of the rust.","topic":"chemistry.reactions","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Chemical change and conservation of mass. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.reactions.e.004","deckId":"chemistry.reactions","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What are the starting substances in a chemical reaction called?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Products","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Catalysts only","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Inert labels","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Reactants"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Reactants are the starting substances that change during a reaction. Products are the substances formed.","scienceFact":"Reactants are the starting substances that change during a reaction. Products are the substances formed.","topic":"chemistry.reactions","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Chemical change and conservation of mass. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.reactions.e.005","deckId":"chemistry.reactions","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What are substances formed by a reaction called?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Products"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Reactants","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Atomic numbers","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Energy levels","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.5.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Products are the substances formed by a chemical reaction. They are written after the arrow in an equation.","scienceFact":"Products are the substances formed by a chemical reaction. They are written after the arrow in an equation.","topic":"chemistry.reactions","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Chemical change and conservation of mass. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"chemistry.reactions.e.006","deckId":"chemistry.reactions","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is changed to balance a chemical equation?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Atomic charges at random","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Coefficients"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Element symbols","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.6.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Formula subscripts","misconception":"chemistry.reactions.mixup.6.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Balancing changes coefficients in front of formulas. Changing subscripts changes the substances in the reaction.","scienceFact":"Balancing changes coefficients in front of formulas. Changing subscripts changes the substances in the reaction.","topic":"chemistry.reactions","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Chemical change and conservation of mass. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claim