their texture.","topic":"earth.rocks","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Rock formation, weathering and the water cycle. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"earth.rocks.m.002","deckId":"earth.rocks","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"Roots grow in cracks beside Philippine rice terraces and break rock apart. What process is this?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Condensation","misconception":"earth.rocks.mixup.2.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Nuclear fusion","misconception":"earth.rocks.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Weathering"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Only erosion","misconception":"earth.rocks.mixup.2.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"Weathering breaks down rock in place. Erosion transports the loosened material elsewhere.","scienceFact":"Weathering breaks down rock in place. Erosion transports the loosened material elsewhere.","topic":"earth.rocks","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Rock formation, weathering and the water cycle. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"earth.rocks.m.003","deckId":"earth.rocks","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"Heavy rain washes soil downhill near a Philippine rice field. What transport process is this?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only weathering in place","misconception":"earth.rocks.mixup.3.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Only crystallization","misconception":"earth.rocks.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Only condensation","misconception":"earth.rocks.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Erosion"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Erosion moves rock or soil by agents such as water, wind, ice or gravity. Plant cover can help reduce it.","scienceFact":"Erosion moves rock or soil by agents such as water, wind, ice or gravity. Plant cover can help reduce it.","topic":"earth.rocks","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"appl