solar.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Moon phases","misconception":"earth.solar.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Daily cloud shape","misconception":"earth.solar.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Axial tilt"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Earth’s tilted axis changes day length and the angle of sunlight during the year. Distance from the Sun is not the main cause of seasons.","scienceFact":"Earth’s tilted axis changes day length and the angle of sunlight during the year. Distance from the Sun is not the main cause of seasons.","topic":"earth.solar","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Planetary motion, moon phases, eclipses and seasons. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"earth.solar.e.005","deckId":"earth.solar","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is Pluto classified as?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Dwarf planet"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Main-sequence star","misconception":"earth.solar.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Earth’s moon","misconception":"earth.solar.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Gas giant","misconception":"earth.solar.mixup.5.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Pluto is a dwarf planet. It is not one of the eight planets in the current Solar System classification.","scienceFact":"Pluto is a dwarf planet. It is not one of the eight planets in the current Solar System classification.","topic":"earth.solar","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Planetary motion, moon phases, eclipses and seasons. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"earth.solar.e.006","deckId":"earth.solar","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What motion causes day and night?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Changing star size","misconception":"earth.solar.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Earth’s rotation"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Earth’s r