nd direction is measured with a wind vane or similar sensor.","topic":"earth.weather","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Atmosphere, monsoons, tropical cyclones and climate change. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"earth.weather.h.010","deckId":"earth.weather","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"Rising air cools and its water vapor forms tiny liquid drops. Which change releases latent heat?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Melting","misconception":"earth.weather.mixup.10.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Sublimation only","misconception":"earth.weather.mixup.10.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Boiling","misconception":"earth.weather.mixup.10.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Condensation"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Cloud droplets can form by condensation as moist air cools. Water vapor itself is an invisible gas.","scienceFact":"Cloud droplets can form by condensation as moist air cools. Water vapor itself is an invisible gas.","topic":"earth.weather","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Atmosphere, monsoons, tropical cyclones and climate change. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"earth.weather.h.011","deckId":"earth.weather","level":"hard","type":"order","prompt":"Order these scales from one short event to a long-term climate pattern.","options":[{"id":"step-0","text":"An afternoon shower"},{"id":"step-1","text":"A rainy week"},{"id":"step-2","text":"Decades of rainfall records"}],"answer":["step-0","step-1","step-2"],"explanation":"An afternoon shower. A rainy week. Decades of rainfall records. Each stage leads to the next.","scienceFact":"Humidity describes water vapor in air. Relative humidity compares it with the amount needed for saturation at that temperature.","topic":"earth.weather","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Atmosphere, monsoons,