h equal allele chances. What percent of offspring are expected to be Aa?","answer":"50","explanation":"The first parent passes A or a equally; the second passes a. Half the expected pairs are Aa.","scienceFact":"The first parent passes A or a equally; the second passes a. Half the expected pairs are Aa.","topic":"life.genetics","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Heredity, variation and natural selection. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true,"unit":"%","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"life.genetics.h.004","deckId":"life.genetics","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A parent produces both A and a gametes at one gene. Which term fits its Aa genotype?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Identical alleles","misconception":"life.genetics.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Heterozygous"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Homozygous","misconception":"life.genetics.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Recessive only","misconception":"life.genetics.mixup.4.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"A heterozygous genotype has two different alleles at the same gene location.","scienceFact":"A heterozygous genotype has two different alleles at the same gene location.","topic":"life.genetics","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Heredity, variation and natural selection. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"life.genetics.h.005","deckId":"life.genetics","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"If gametes kept the full chromosome number, it would double at fertilization. Which division prevents this?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Osmosis","misconception":"life.genetics.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Budding","misconception":"life.genetics.mixup.5.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Meiosis"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Mitosis","misconception":"life.genetics.mixup.5.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"M