","answer":"9","explanation":"Kinetic energy = ½mv² = ½ × 2 × 3² = 9 J. Squaring the speed is essential.","scienceFact":"Kinetic energy = ½mv² = ½ × 2 × 3² = 9 J. Squaring the speed is essential.","topic":"physics.energy","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Mechanical energy, heat transfer and power. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true,"unit":"J","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.energy.h.002","deckId":"physics.energy","level":"hard","type":"calc","prompt":"A farmer lifts a 4 kg rice sack 2 m above a reference level. Use g = 10 m/s². How much gravitational potential energy is added?","answer":"80","explanation":"Potential energy added = mgh = 4 × 10 × 2 = 80 J.","scienceFact":"Potential energy added = mgh = 4 × 10 × 2 = 80 J.","topic":"physics.energy","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Mechanical energy, heat transfer and power. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true,"unit":"J","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.energy.h.003","deckId":"physics.energy","level":"hard","type":"calc","prompt":"A Cebu student does 120 J of work in 6 s. What is the average power?","answer":"20","explanation":"Average power = work ÷ time = 120 ÷ 6 = 20 W.","scienceFact":"Average power = work ÷ time = 120 ÷ 6 = 20 W.","topic":"physics.energy","gradeBand":10,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Mechanical energy, heat transfer and power. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true,"unit":"W","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.energy.h.004","deckId":"physics.energy","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A device transfers 600 J in 3 s rather than 6 s. Which rate is larger in the faster transfer?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Distance only","misconception":"physics.energy.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Power"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Ma