calc","prompt":"A Cebu lab cart has mass 3 kg and speeds up at 4 m/s². What net force is needed?","answer":"12","explanation":"Newton’s second law gives net force = mass × acceleration = 3 × 4 = 12 N.","scienceFact":"Newton’s second law gives net force = mass × acceleration = 3 × 4 = 12 N.","topic":"physics.forces","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Newton’s laws, friction, gravity and net force. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true,"unit":"N","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.forces.h.003","deckId":"physics.forces","level":"hard","type":"calc","prompt":"A Philippine rice sack has mass 5 kg. Use g = 10 m/s². What is its weight near Earth’s surface?","answer":"50","explanation":"Weight = mass × gravitational acceleration = 5 × 10 = 50 N. Mass and weight use different units.","scienceFact":"Weight = mass × gravitational acceleration = 5 × 10 = 50 N. Mass and weight use different units.","topic":"physics.forces","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"Newton’s laws, friction, gravity and net force. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true,"unit":"N","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.forces.h.004","deckId":"physics.forces","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A box feels several pushes and pulls. Which quantity must be found to predict its acceleration?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Elapsed time","misconception":"physics.forces.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Net force"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Single action-reaction pair","misconception":"physics.forces.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Body volume","misconception":"physics.forces.mixup.4.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Net force is the vector sum of forces on one object. It determines the object’s acceleration.","scienceFact":"Net force is the vector sum of forces on one object. It determines the object’s acceleration.","to