not need a material medium. Sound, by contrast, is a mechanical wave that requires matter.","topic":"physics.light","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Reflection, refraction and electromagnetic radiation. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"physics.light.e.003","deckId":"physics.light","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What happens when light reflects from a plane mirror?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"The incoming angle must be zero","misconception":"physics.light.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"The two angles sum to 180°","misconception":"physics.light.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"The two angles are equal"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"The reflected angle is twice as large","misconception":"physics.light.mixup.3.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"The angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection. Both angles are measured from the normal to the surface.","scienceFact":"The angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection. Both angles are measured from the normal to the surface.","topic":"physics.light","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Reflection, refraction and electromagnetic radiation. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"physics.light.e.004","deckId":"physics.light","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is a change in light’s direction when it enters a different medium called?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only reflection","misconception":"physics.light.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Combustion","misconception":"physics.light.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Sound absorption","misconception":"physics.light.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Refraction"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Refraction occurs when a wave changes speed between media. At an angle, this usually changes its direction too.","scienceFa