","text":"Accuracy by definition","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.9.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Large random variation","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.9.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"High uncertainty by definition","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.9.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Precise readings are close to one another. They can still miss the true value if a tool has a bias.","scienceFact":"Precise readings are close to one another. They can still miss the true value if a tool has a bias.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.e.010","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the SI derived unit for volume?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Kilogram per meter","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.10.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Cubic meter"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Square meter","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.10.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Meter per second","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.10.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Volume is three-dimensional space. The coherent SI unit is the cubic meter, written m³.","scienceFact":"Volume is three-dimensional space. The coherent SI unit is the cubic meter, written m³.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"diagram":"measure"},{"id":"skills.measurement.e.011","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What scale feature is the smallest change an instrument can show?","answer":"Resolution","explanation":"Resolution is the smallest change an instrument can distinguish or display. It limits the detail available in a reading.","scienceFact":"Resolution is the smallest change an instrument can distinguish or display. It limits the detail available in a reading.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"accept":["resolution","Resolution"]},{"id":"skills.measurement.e.012","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What process compares a tool’s readings against known standards?","answer":"Calibration","explanation":"Calibration checks readings against known standards. This can show if a tool has a bias or needs to be adjusted.","scienceFact":"Calibration checks readings against known standards. This can show if a tool has a bias or needs to be adjusted.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"accept":["calibration","Calibration"]},{"id":"skills.measurement.m.001","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A Philippine class records a rice plot’s length using the SI base unit. Which unit should be used?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Kelvin","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.1.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Meter"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Kilogram","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Second","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.1.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"The meter is the SI base unit of length. One meter equals one hundred centimeters.","scienceFact":"The meter is the SI base unit of length. One meter equals one hundred centimeters.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply