usand grams. The prefix kilo- means one thousand.","scienceFact":"One kilogram equals one thousand grams. The prefix kilo- means one thousand.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.006","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A temperature must be expressed on the absolute SI scale before taking a gas-law ratio. Which unit fits?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Degree Celsius only","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.6.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Joule","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.6.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Watt","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Kelvin"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Kelvin is the SI base unit of thermodynamic temperature. Gas-law ratios use absolute temperature in kelvin.","scienceFact":"Kelvin is the SI base unit of thermodynamic temperature. Gas-law ratios use absolute temperature in kelvin.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.007","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"Two readings differ when the observer looks from above or below a meniscus. Which eye position reduces this parallax error?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"At the meniscus level"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Far above the cylinder","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.7.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Far below the cylinder","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.7.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Facing away from the scale","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.7.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Read a liquid scale at eye level to reduce parallax. For water in common glassware, read the bottom of the curved meniscus.","scienceFact":"Read a liquid scale at eye level to reduce parallax. For water in common glassware, read the bottom of the curved meniscus.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.008","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A set of readings clusters far from the true value. Which measurement quality is poor despite close grouping?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only speed","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.8.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Accuracy"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Only precision","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.8.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Only sample size","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.8.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Accuracy concerns closeness to a true or accepted value. Precision concerns the spread of repeated measurements.","scienceFact":"Accuracy concerns closeness to a true or accepted value. Precision concerns the spread of repeated measurements.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.009","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"Readings of 9.9, 10.0 and 10.1 cm have little spread, though the reference is 12 cm. Which quality is high?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Large random variation","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.9.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"High uncertainty by definition","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.9.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Precision"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Accuracy by definition","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.9.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"Precise readings are close to one another. They can still miss the true value if a tool has a bias.","scienceFact":"Precise readings are close to one another. They can still miss the true value if a tool has a bias.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.010","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"Multiplying 2 m × 3 m × 4 m gives 24 of which volume unit?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Square meter","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.10.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Meter per second","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.10.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Kilogram per meter","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.10.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Cubic meter"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Volume is three-dimensional space. The coherent SI unit is the cubic meter, written m³.","scienceFact":"Volume is three-dimensional space. The coherent SI unit is the cubic meter, written m³.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.011","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"order","prompt":"Put these steps in order to use a balance.","options":[{"id":"step-0","text":"Place the balance level"},{"id":"step-1","text":"Zero the balance"},{"id":"step-2","text":"Add the sample"},{"id":"step-3","text":"Record mass with units"}],"answer":["step-0","step-1","step-2","step-3"],"explanation":"Place the balance level. Zero the balance. Add the sample. Record mass with units. Each stage leads to the next.","scienceFact":"Resolution is the smallest change an instrument can distinguish or display. It limits the detail available in a reading.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.measurement.h.012","deckId":"skills.measurement","level":"hard","type":"diagram","prompt":"A tool is checked at several known values and adjusted if needed. Which process improves trust in its readings?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Photosynthesis","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.12.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Calibration"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Evaporation","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.12.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Magnetization only","misconception":"skills.measurement.mixup.12.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Calibration checks readings against known standards. This can show if a tool has a bias or needs to be adjusted.","scienceFact":"Calibration checks readings against known standards. This can show if a tool has a bias or needs to be adjusted.","topic":"skills.measurement","gradeBand":9,"bloom":"analyze","curriculumArea":"SI units, measurement, uncertainty and conversions. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"diagram":"measure"},{"id":"skills.method.e.001","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is a science idea that can be tested with evidence called?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Hypothesis"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Unchangeable truth","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Personal taste only","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.1.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Final proof with no test","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.1.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"A hypothesis is a testable explanation or prediction. Evidence can support it or show that it needs to change.","scienceFact":"A hypothesis is a testable explanation or prediction. Evidence can support it or show that it needs to change.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.002","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What variable does a student deliberately change in a fair test?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Final conclusion","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Independent variable"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Dependent variable","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.2.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Unmeasured opinion","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.2.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"The independent variable is deliberately changed or compared. It may affect the measured outcome.","scienceFact":"The independent variable is deliberately changed or compared. It may affect the measured outcome.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.003","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What variable is measured as the outcome of a test?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Controlled pot size","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Unrelated label","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Dependent variable"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Independent variable","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.3.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"The dependent variable is the measured outcome. It may change in response to the independent variable.","scienceFact":"The dependent variable is the measured outcome. It may change in response to the independent variable.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.004","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What should usually happen to other important conditions in a fair test?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Change them all at once","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Ignore them completely","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Choose them after seeing results","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Keep them controlled"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"Controlling other conditions helps isolate the effect of the variable being tested.","scienceFact":"Controlling other conditions helps isolate the effect of the variable being tested.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.005","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"Why should a test be repeated?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"To check consistency and reduce random effects"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"To guarantee a desired result","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"To erase every difference","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"To avoid recording evidence","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.5.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Repeated trials reveal variation and improve confidence in a pattern. They do not guarantee that a claim is true.","scienceFact":"Repeated trials reveal variation and improve confidence in a pattern. They do not guarantee that a claim is true.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.006","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What should a conclusion be based on?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only the loudest voice","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Recorded evidence"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Only personal preference","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.6.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Only the first guess","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.6.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Base the conclusion on the data. This still matters when the result differs from your first prediction.","scienceFact":"Base the conclusion on the data. This still matters when the result differs from your first prediction.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.007","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is a detailed description of how a test is carried out called?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Opinion section","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.7.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Title only","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.7.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Procedure"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Result alone","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.7.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"A clear procedure describes what was done so others can repeat and assess the test.","scienceFact":"A clear procedure describes what was done so others can repeat and assess the test.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.008","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"Which kind of question can be tested in a school investigation?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Which plant is the prettiest?","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.8.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Is green the nicest color?","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.8.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Are flowers better than stories?","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.8.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"How does light duration affect seedling height?"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"A testable question links conditions that can be measured or compared. Personal preferences are not tested in the same way.","scienceFact":"A testable question links conditions that can be measured or compared. Personal preferences are not tested in the same way.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.009","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What makes a comparison group useful?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Whether the treatment made a difference"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Whether the result is guaranteed","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.9.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Whether measurements can be skipped","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.9.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Whether all plants are identical","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.9.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"A comparison group shows what happens without the treatment. It helps us judge whether the treatment caused a change.","scienceFact":"A comparison group shows what happens without the treatment. It helps us judge whether the treatment caused a change.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.e.010","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What should a student do with data that do not match a prediction?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Hide the whole method","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.10.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Keep it and investigate"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Delete it to fit the guess","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.10.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Change its value secretly","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.10.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Keep valid data, even when they surprise you. Check the method and test again to learn what may have caused the result.","scienceFact":"Keep valid data, even when they surprise you. Check the method and test again to learn what may have caused the result.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"diagram":"lab"},{"id":"skills.method.e.011","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What is a record made with senses or tools called?","answer":"Observation","explanation":"An observation is a record made with senses or tools. An inference is an explanation drawn from evidence.","scienceFact":"An observation is a record made with senses or tools. An inference is an explanation drawn from evidence.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"accept":["observation","Observation"]},{"id":"skills.method.e.012","deckId":"skills.method","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What scientific habit means changing a claim when good new evidence disagrees?","answer":"Revise the explanation","explanation":"Science is open to revision. Stronger evidence can lead to a better explanation or a changed model.","scienceFact":"Science is open to revision. Stronger evidence can lead to a better explanation or a changed model.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":7,"bloom":"remember","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true,"accept":["revise the explanation","Revise the explanation"]},{"id":"skills.method.m.001","deckId":"skills.method","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A Philippine class predicts that rice seedlings grow taller with more light. What kind of testable idea is this?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Final proof with no test","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.1.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Hypothesis"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Unchangeable truth","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Personal taste only","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.1.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"A hypothesis is a testable explanation or prediction. Evidence can support it or show that it needs to change.","scienceFact":"A hypothesis is a testable explanation or prediction. Evidence can support it or show that it needs to change.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.m.002","deckId":"skills.method","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A Philippine class changes only the light hours given to rice plants. What variable is light duration?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Unmeasured opinion","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.2.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Final conclusion","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Independent variable"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Dependent variable","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.2.1"}],"answer":"choice-2","explanation":"The independent variable is deliberately changed or compared. It may affect the measured outcome.","scienceFact":"The independent variable is deliberately changed or compared. It may affect the measured outcome.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.m.003","deckId":"skills.method","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A Cebu class measures rice seedling height after changing light hours. What variable is plant height?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Independent variable","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.3.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Controlled pot size","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Unrelated label","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Dependent variable"}],"answer":"choice-3","explanation":"The dependent variable is the measured outcome. It may change in response to the independent variable.","scienceFact":"The dependent variable is the measured outcome. It may change in response to the independent variable.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":true,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.m.004","deckId":"skills.method","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A class tests water amount but keeps seed type, soil and light alike. What role do those unchanged conditions have?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Keep them controlled"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Change them all at once","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Ignore them completely","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Choose them after seeing results","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.4.3"}],"answer":"choice-0","explanation":"Controlling other conditions helps isolate the effect of the variable being tested.","scienceFact":"Controlling other conditions helps isolate the effect of the variable being tested.","topic":"skills.method","gradeBand":8,"bloom":"apply","curriculumArea":"Testable questions, fair tests, evidence and variables. Content aligns with these curriculum areas; no official competency codes are claimed.","ph":false,"reviewed":true},{"id":"skills.method.m.005","deckId":"skills.method","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"Three trials give slightly different results. Why repeat the test rather than trust one trial?","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"To avoid recording evidence","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.5.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"To check consistency and reduce random effects"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"To guarantee a desired result","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"To erase every difference","misconception":"skills.method.mixup.5.2"}],"answer":"choice-1","explanation":"Repeated trials reveal variation and improve confidence in a pattern. They do not guarantee that a claim is true.","scienceFact":"Repeated trials reveal variation and improve confidence in a pattern. They do not guarantee that a claim is true.","t